  "live_records": {
    "q-124153": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124153",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u+v-1,\\,y=-u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(-3,1)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+v-1 \\\\ -u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+v \\\\ -u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$ \n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(-12,1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
